Surface the print agent's real error instead of a blanket "not
reachable", show APC's short consignment number (v0.131)

Dan tested Print Label on a real APC order right after v0.130 and saw
nothing happen - no tab, no print, matching what's *supposed* to happen
when the print agent (print-agent/agent.py, a small local Python/Windows-
tray tool BNS already built for exactly this - not QZ Tray, which came up
as something used with APC in the past but isn't what this app talks to)
isn't reachable. Its ZPL handling is already generic (any courier's raw
bytes, not DPD-specific), so no backend change was needed there - but
digging into the actual failure path in printAgent.ts found a real bug:
when the agent IS running and reachable but the print itself fails inside
it (pywin32 not installed, the printer name in Settings not matching what
Windows calls it, SumatraPDF missing, the printer offline, ...), the agent
already replies with its own {"status":"error","message":"..."} body
explaining exactly why - but the frontend discarded that response entirely
and reported the same generic "Print agent not reachable" message either
way, so a real, fixable problem looked identical to "the agent just isn't
running". printPdf/printRaw now read that body back out when the agent did
respond (just not with 2xx) and both DPD and APC's Print Label, plus Print
Picking Note, surface the agent's own reason - the generic message is now
only shown for a genuine connection failure.

Also: Dan found the "consignment number" APC's own portal shows
(0007051) is simply the last 7 digits of the full 22-digit Hypaship
WayBill this app stores - now shown alongside the waybill on the order
screen so it doesn't need re-deriving by hand every time it's needed for
a phone call or the portal.

